      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "The number of vegetarian options is given as 4. The fraction of the menu that is vegetarian is given as [vegetarian_dishes / num_of_dishes] = 0.25.\n\nAmong the vegetarian items, 3 are made with pasta, a type of gluten. The fraction of vegetarian dishes that contain gluten is then given by 3/4.\n\nThe fraction of the entire menu that you can eat, which includes both the vegetarian and non-vegetarian dishes but excluding those with gluten, can be calculated as [(vegetarian_dishes - gluten_dishes) / [vegetarian_dishes / num_of_dishes]] = 0.05.\n\nThus, the fraction of the entire menu that you can eat is 0.05 = 1/20.The full reasoning steps for this sum are as follows:\n\n1. Given the total number of vegetarian dishes is 4 and 1/5th of the menu's total dishes. \n2. We know that the number of vegetarian dishes is 4, and this represents 1/5 of the menu, so we can determine the total number of dishes by diving the number of vegetarian dishes by the fraction 1/5:\n   4 / (1/5) = 4 * 5 = 20\n\n3. Out of these 20 total dishes, there are 3 dishes which contain gluten (3 are made with pasta).\n4. We need to determine how many among the vegetarian dishes can be eaten as vegetarian but without any gluten. Thus, subtracting the number of gluten-containing vegetarian dishes:\n   4 - 3 = 1\n   This is 1/20th of the total dishes.\n\n5. Finally, to confirm - 4/total_dishes = 1/20\n\nSo, 1/20th of the entire menu consists of the items you can eat.\n\nTherefore, the final answer, as requested, is 1/20.",
